    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "SOUTH FACING REAR GARDEN.\r\nQUIET CUL DE SAC SETTING.\r\nENORMOUS POTENTIAL TO EXTEND TO SIDE AND REAR SUBJECT TO P.P.\r\nGARAGE SPACE SUITABLE FOR CONVERSION.\r\nGAS FIRED CENTRAL HEATING – NEW COMBI BOILER NOV 2021.\r\nBATHROOM, KITCHEN, INC. FLOORS AND APPLIANCES, INSTALLED 2017.\r\nCITY VIEWS TO HOWTH, CONVENTION CENTRE, SPIRE FROM FIRST FLOOR. \r\nOPEN PLAN DOWNSTAIRS WITH NATURAL FLOW TO THE GARDEN - AN EXCELLENT SPACE FOR ENTERTAINING.\r\nOFF STREET DRIVEWAY PARKING.\r\nLUAS WITHIN A SHORT WALK.\r\nMINUTES DRIVE TO M50.\r\nDUNDRUM VILLAGE ON THE DOORSTEP.\r\n\r\n\r\nWelcome to this bright and spacious three-bedroom semi-detached family home, offering approximately 91sq.m of living space plus garage measuring approx. 13.6sq.m. Built c.1967, this property has been beautifully maintained and upgraded in recent years.  One of the standout features of this home is the large, south facing, private rear garden, providing ample space for outdoor activities and relaxation. The property features gas fired central heating with a new combi boiler installed in 2021. \r\n\r\nUpon entering, the ground floor comprises a comfortable living room and a well appointed kitchen/dining room with sliding door leading to the rear garden.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, there are three generous bedrooms, each offering a tranquil and comfortable space. Completing the accommodation is a main shower room and guest w.c. downstairs.\r\n\r\nWithin close proximity, you'll find the vibrant villages of Dundrum and Churchtown, offering a range of shops, restaurants, and entertainment options. Families will appreciate the abundance of crèches, primary schools and secondary schools in the local area, ensuring quality education for children.\r\n\r\nFor shopping enthusiasts, the renowned Dundrum Town Centre is within a short walk, offering an extensive selection of retail outlets and entertainment facilities. Additionally, the Dundrum LUAS stop is conveniently located within a 10 minute walk, providing efficient access to the city centre and beyond.\r\n\r\nThis property presents an exceptional opportunity to own a well-maintained family home in a prime location with an array of amenities right at your doorstep.\r\n\r\n\r\nAccommodation\r\n\r\nPorch: Wooden venetian blinds, tiled floor, door to\r\n\r\nGuest W.c.: W.c., pedestal w.h.b., wall mirror, recessed lighting, tiled floor.\r\n\r\nLiving Room: Open fireplace with attractive surround and timber mantel, fitted shelving, wall lighting, under stairs storage, double doors to \r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining Room: Fully fitted kitchen with comprehensive range of wall and base units, breakfast seating area, Climote control, Whirlpool oven, Bosch hob, stainless steel extractor hood, dishwasher, tiled splashback, fitted shelving, wall lighting, door to side and sliding patio doors to rear garden.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor:\r\n\r\nLanding: Recessed lighting, carpet.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1: Fitted wardrobes and storage, wooden venetian blinds, carpet.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2: Fitted storage, shelving and hanging space, vanity area, access to attic, carpet.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3: Carpet.\r\n\r\nShower Room: Double wide shower with rainfall showerhead, w.c. with concealed cistern, w.h.b. with under vanity storage, heated towel rail, tiled floor and walls. \r\n\r\nExterior:  \r\n\r\nGarage: Approx. 13.6sq.m.  Up and over door, Glow-worm gas boiler (installed Nov 2021), plumbed for washing machine, power and lighting.\r\n\r\nRear garden: South facing, access to garage, two block built storage sheds, patio area, electric sockets, landscaped garden with lawn, vegetable garden, mature trees and shrubs, side access.\r\n\r\nFront garden: Off-street driveway parking, lawn, mature shrubs and planting, side access."
      },
